1 0 0 1 54 646 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 54 630 Tm (Thisproject is a real-time command-line ASCII survival game written in F# using .NET 10.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 614 Tm (The user plays as a passenger trapped on a moving train during a zombie outbreak. The) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 598 Tm (user must move forward through five train cars, avoid or defeat zombies, and reach the) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 582 Tm (engine before losing all HP.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 566 Tm () Tj
/F2 14 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 550 Tm (Requirements) Tj
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 530 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 54 514 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 54 498 Tm (1. When the program starts, it will display a narrative intro in the terminal and wait) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 482 Tm (   for the user to press `Enter` before gameplay begins.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 466 Tm (2. During gameplay, the game will run in a continuous real-time loop and redraw the) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 450 Tm (   terminal repeatedly without requiring the user to press `Enter` for each action.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 434 Tm (3. Each train car will be rendered as an ASCII frame using `+`, `-`, and `|` around an) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 418 Tm (   internal playable area.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 402 Tm (4. The internal playable area of each train car will be `18` columns wide and `4` rows) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 386 Tm (   tall.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 370 Tm (5. The game will contain exactly five train cars. The user wins by advancing through all) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 354 Tm (   five cars and reaching the engine.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 338 Tm (6. The game will use the following symbols during gameplay:) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 322 Tm (   - `P` for the player) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 306 Tm (   - `Z` for a zombie) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 290 Tm (   - `*` for the projectile) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 274 Tm (   - `#` for a seat or obstacle) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 258 Tm (   - `D` for the door to the next car) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 242 Tm (   - space for an empty floor tile) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 226 Tm (7. The user will control the player with the keyboard during gameplay. Pressing `W`,) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 210 Tm (   `A`, `S`, or `D` will move the player up, left, down, or right. The arrow keys will) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 194 Tm (   also move the player in the corresponding direction.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 178 Tm (8. Moving the player will also change the player's facing direction to the direction of) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 162 Tm (   movement, even if the attempted movement is blocked.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 146 Tm (9. The player cannot move outside the playable grid, through obstacles, or through) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 130 Tm (   zombies.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 114 Tm (10. The player starts with `3` HP. If HP reaches `0`, the game ends in a loss.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 98 Tm (11. Pressing `Space` will launch the projectile in the player's current facing direction) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 82 Tm (    only if the projectile is in the `READY` state.) Tj
ET
endstream
