stream
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 738 Tm (12. The player can have only one projectile. While the projectile is in flight, pressing) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 722 Tm (    `Space` again will not create another projectile.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 706 Tm (13. If the projectile moves into a zombie, that zombie will be removed, the player's) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 690 Tm (    score will increase by `1`, and the projectile will begin returning toward the) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 674 Tm (    player.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 658 Tm (14. If the projectile moves into an obstacle or the edge of the train car, it will) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 642 Tm (    reverse into a returning state instead of disappearing.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 626 Tm (15. When the returning projectile reaches the player, the projectile state becomes) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 610 Tm (    `READY` again and the player may shoot again.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 594 Tm (16. Pressing `R` while the projectile is in flight and not already returning will force) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 578 Tm (    the projectile to start returning toward the player.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 562 Tm (17. Each train car will begin with a fixed number of zombies:) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 546 Tm (   - Car 1: `1` zombie) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 530 Tm (   - Car 2: `2` zombies) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 514 Tm (   - Car 3: `3` zombies) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 498 Tm (   - Car 4: `4` zombies) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 482 Tm (   - Car 5: `5` zombies) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 466 Tm (18. Zombies will move toward the player automatically at a slower interval than the) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 450 Tm (    screen refresh.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 434 Tm (19. Zombies cannot move through obstacles, outside the playable grid, through the exit) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 418 Tm (    door tile, or onto another zombie's position.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 402 Tm (20. If a zombie reaches the player's position, the player loses `1` HP and that zombie) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 386 Tm (    is removed from the train car.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 370 Tm (21. The door `D` to the next car will remain closed while at least one zombie remains in) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 354 Tm (    the current car.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 338 Tm (22. When the last zombie in the current car is defeated, the door will open.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 322 Tm (23. If the player moves onto the open door tile, the game will load the next train car,) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 306 Tm (    reset the player to the next car's entry position, and reset the projectile to) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 290 Tm (    `READY`.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 274 Tm (24. After entering the fifth car's exit, the game will display a win ending.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 258 Tm (25. Each gameplay frame will display the train car map, a status line, a message line or) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 242 Tm (    block, and a controls reminder.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 226 Tm (26. The status display will show the player's HP, projectile state, score, and current) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 210 Tm (    car number.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 194 Tm (27. The message area will show short event-driven narrative updates for important events) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 178 Tm (    such as defeating a zombie, unlocking a door, advancing to the next car, winning, or) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 162 Tm (    losing.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 146 Tm (28. Pressing `Q` during gameplay will quit the program.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 130 Tm (29. After a win or loss, pressing `Enter` will restart the game from the beginning.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 114 Tm (30. The game's car layouts, zombie placements, and obstacle placements will be fixed) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 98 Tm (    rather than random so that the game behavior remains deterministic and testable.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 82 Tm () Tj
ET
endstream
